/**
 * @module test/fixtures/guardrail-corpus
 *
 * Labeled snippets for the guardrail rules (hardening 4.5).
 *
 * Every entry is one rule and one snippet, labeled `bad` when the rule has to
 * fire and `good` when it must stay silent. The pairing is the point: a rule
 * that only ever sees violations can be made to pass by firing on everything,
 * and a rule that only ever sees idiomatic code can be made to pass by firing
 * on nothing. Ten rules were fixed by hand in 4.1 and this is the net under
 * those fixes.
 *
 * A snippet is judged on its target rule alone. Most of them trip some other
 * rule as well - real code does - and that is not what the entry is measuring.
 *
 * `skill` picks which rule set the snippet is checked against, because a rule
 * only runs for the skills that carry it.
 */

